# Settings Clarchy reads from the environment. Copy this file to .env (git ignores it),
# uncomment and fill in what you need, and load it into your shell before running Clarchy:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#     clarchy serve
#
# Clarchy does not read .env by itself. Leave everything commented out to plan with the
# rule-based planner, which needs no key and no network. Keep unused lines commented: an
# empty value is not always the same as unset (CLARCHY_PRICES_DIR= turns off refreshed
# price books, for example).

# ---- Which model plans (src/clarchy/planner/llm.py) ----
# anthropic | bedrock | huggingface | ollama | openai-compatible | rules
# Unset: anthropic when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, huggingface when HF_TOKEN is set,
# otherwise rules.
# CLARCHY_LLM=
# The model id. Unset uses the backend's default: DEFAULT_MODEL in llm.py (anthropic; on
# bedrock with the "anthropic." prefix), Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct (huggingface) or
# qwen2.5:7b (ollama). Required for openai-compatible.
# CLARCHY_MODEL=

# Claude through the Claude API.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Claude on Amazon Bedrock uses your usual AWS credentials (AWS_PROFILE or access keys)
# and this region (or AWS_DEFAULT_REGION).
# AWS_REGION=

# Open-source models through Hugging Face Inference Providers. A free token works:
# https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens (allow "Make calls to Inference Providers").
# HF_TOKEN=

# Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio or any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint. For ollama the URL
# defaults to http://localhost:11434/v1 and no key is needed.
# CLARCHY_LLM_BASE_URL=
# CLARCHY_LLM_API_KEY=

# ---- Serving ----
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call `clarchy serve` from a site hosted elsewhere.
# CLARCHY_CORS_ORIGINS=

# ---- Prices and icons (optional) ----
# Folder of price books written by `clarchy prices update` (default ~/.cache/clarchy/prices).
# CLARCHY_PRICES_DIR=
# 1 makes `make prices` refresh the price books from the providers' APIs (slow).
# CLARCHY_REFRESH_PRICES=
# A Google Cloud API key with the Cloud Billing API enabled. Only
# `python -m clarchy.gcp_prices --discover` reads it; Google Cloud prices are still
# compiled by hand.
# GCP_API_KEY=
# Folders of a provider's own icon package, used instead of the icons Clarchy ships.
# CLARCHY_ICONS_AWS=
# CLARCHY_ICONS_AZURE=
# CLARCHY_ICONS_GCP=
